<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-BG Bank ups Denmark's 1996 GDP &amp; CPI.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-BG Bank ups Denmark's 1996 GDP &amp; CPI.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey Denmark's third-biggest bank BG Bank on Thursday upped its expectations for Denmark's 1996 GDP (gross domestic product) growth to 2.3 percent from 2.0 percent in its last forecast in July.</p>
<p>At the same time it raised its 1996 forecast for inflation to 2.1 percent from 2.0 percent, upwardly adjusting its estimate for the current account surplus to 8.0 billion crowns from 6.0 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The latest Danish Economy Ministry forecast in October foresaw 2.0 percent GDP growth, 2.1 percent inflation, 8.9 percent unemployment and a current account surplus of 10.3 billion crowns for this year.</p>
<p>The following estimates were made by 10 leading local and international organisations.</p>
<p>		(pct)  GDP    inflation unemployment  c/a (bln crns)</p>
<p>BG Bank (10/96)    2.3    2.1	  8.9	     8.0</p>
<p>Codan Bank (10/96) 2.3    2.2	  8.9	    10.0</p>
<p>Sydbank (10/96)    2.0    2.1	  9.4	    10.0</p>
<p>Morgan St (10/96)  1.9    2.1	  9.0	    10.0</p>
<p>Paribas (9/96)     1.6    2.2	  --	     17.7</p>
<p>Danske Bank (9/96) 1.2    2.1	  9.0	     7.4</p>
<p>PaineWebber (9/96) 1.7    2.1	  8.5	     8.1</p>
<p>Citibank (9/96)    1.1    2.2	  7.7	     7.5</p>
<p>NatWest  (9/96)    1.5    2.1	  9.0	     6.9</p>
<p>Chase M (9/96)     1.5    1.9	  --		8.0</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
